Package: gettoken-parse
Architecture: any
Static-Built-Using: ${misc:Static-Built-Using}
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}@DEPENDS@:gettoken-parse
Description: token broker for AI agents - reads a document through its contract
 parse reads one document on standard input, checks it against the contract
 named on its command line, and hands back the fields asked for as assignments
 a shell can evaluate. A document that does not satisfy its contract yields
 nothing to evaluate.
 .
 It carries no contract of its own. What may cross a boundary is stated by the
 contract package the component reading that boundary depends on.

Package: gettoken-format
Architecture: any
Static-Built-Using: ${misc:Static-Built-Using}
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}@DEPENDS@:gettoken-format
Description: token broker for AI agents - writes a document through its contract
 format takes the fields named on its command line from the environment, writes
 the document they make, and checks that document against the contract before
 handing it over. A component cannot emit something its contract does not admit.
 .
 It carries no contract of its own, for the same reason parse does not.
